  <h1 class="section-heading">PROGRAM ACCREDITATION</h1>
  <div class="content-body">
    <p>The <span data-field="college_name">{{ college_name }}</span> College Physician Assistant Program is accredited by the <span data-field="accreditation_body">{{ accreditation_body }}</span>. Provisional status to the <span data-field="accreditation_body">{{ accreditation_body }}</span> Physician Assistant Program sponsored by <span data-field="sponsoring_institution">{{ sponsoring_institution }}</span> College.</p>
    <p>Accreditation - Provisional is an accreditation status granted when the plans and resource allocation, if fully implemented as planned, of a proposed program that has not yet enrolled students appear to demonstrate the program's ability to meet the <span data-field="accreditation_standards">{{ accreditation_standards }}</span>. Provisional status appears to demonstrate continued progress in complying with the <span data-field="accreditation_standards">{{ accreditation_standards }}</span> as it prepares for the graduation of the first class (cohort) of students.</p>
    <p>Accreditation - Provisional does not ensure any subsequent accreditation status. It is limited to no more than five years from matriculation of the first class.</p>
    <p>The program's accreditation history can be viewed on the <span data-field="accreditation_website">{{ accreditation_website }}</span> website.</p>
  </div>
</div>

