      <li><strong>Admission:</strong> If selected following the interview, candidates with all prerequisites completed and a bachelor's degree conferred will be recommended for full admission status. Candidates with outstanding requirements that have been selected by the admissions committee will be recommended for conditional/provisional admission status.</li>
      <li><strong>Wait List Candidate:</strong> Alternates to the program will be selected by the admissions committee and placed on the waitlist. As seats in the program become available, students on the waitlist may be offered a seat in the program for admission. Once the program is full, the program will communicate this with remaining students on the waitlist. Students not selected for admission to the program may reapply for subsequent admission cycles if they so choose.</li>
      <li><strong>Denial:</strong> Applicants to the program who have not been selected for admission will be notified in writing and may reapply for subsequent admission cycles if they so choose.</li>
