      <p>Students should anticipate travel out of state for a minimum of two preceptorships, each lasting five weeks in duration.</p>
      <p>Other costs not included in tuition:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>**Equipment List:** Students are encouraged to wait until orientation to purchase equipment (not including smart phone, laptop, or wrist watch). If students already own any of the medical equipment below (i.e. stethoscope or otoscope/ophthalmoscope), approval of the equipment must first be obtained from the PA program director. Welch Allen Package (estimated list below) - Total (estimated) $900.00</li>
        <li>Welch Allen Classic 3.5V Diagnostic Set</li>
        <li>Welch Allen Adult and pediatric blood pressure cuff</li>
        <li>3M Littmann Stethoscope</li>
        <li>Pocket Eye Card with Ruler</li>
        <li>LED Penlight</li>
        <li>Reflex Hammer</li>
        <li>Dissection Kit</li>
        <li>Tape Measure</li>
        <li>Protective Eye Wear</li>
        <li>Medical Bag</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Background Checks/Health Screenings:</strong></p>
      <p>FBI Criminal Background Check and Child Abuse Clearance - $863 each year</p>
      <p>Health Physical/Immunizations Tickers/Drug Screen - varies by insurance carrier***</p>
      <p><strong>Health Insurance Requirements:</strong> In accordance with Elizabethtown College's health insurance requirements, students enrolled in the Elizabethtown PA program are required to maintain personal health insurance for the entire duration of the program. Proof of insurance coverage must be provided prior to orientation. Students are responsible for all personal health care costs incurred while enrolled in the PA program, including any costs incurred in the event of exposure from a contaminated needle stick, puncture wound, or contamination of any obviously open wound or the mucous membranes by saliva, blood, or other bodily fluids. Due to the potential risk for exposure to potentially infectious materials, insurance should cover screenings, diagnostic testing, treatments that may result from any potential exposure. (A3.08)</p>
      <p>Please refer to the <a href="https://www.etown.edu/business-office">Business Office</a> to view policies and procedures for refunds of tuition and fees.</p>
